{"total_count": 20, "incomplete_results": false, "items": [{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/642", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/642/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/642/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/642/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/642", "id": 4669043042, "node_id": "PR_kwDOA-b4g87mvayr", "number": 642, "title": "Add `wait_golden_jitter`: deterministic low-discrepancy jitter strategy", "user": {"login": "F4V3L4", "id": 253787503, "node_id": "U_kgDODyB9bw", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/253787503?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/F4V3L4", "html_url": "https://github.com/F4V3L4", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/F4V3L4/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/F4V3L4/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/F4V3L4/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/F4V3L4/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/F4V3L4/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/F4V3L4/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/F4V3L4/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/F4V3L4/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/F4V3L4/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "open", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 0, "created_at": "2026-06-15T21:28:19Z", "updated_at": "2026-06-16T01:53:00Z", "closed_at": null, "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/pulls/642", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/642", "diff_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/642.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/642.patch", "merged_at": null}, "body": "# Add `wait_golden_jitter`: deterministic low-discrepancy jitter strategy\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR adds a new wait strategy, `wait_golden_jitter`, providing a\n**deterministic** low-discrepancy alternative to the existing random jitter\nstrategies (`wait_random_exponential` / \"Full Jitter\").\n\nIt keeps the same exponentially expanding backoff window as\n`wait_random_exponential`, but selects each waiter's delay from the\ngolden-ratio low-discrepancy sequence (indexed by a caller-supplied\n`seq_index`) instead of drawing it at random.\n\n## Motivation\n\nThe existing jitter strategies break retry synchronization using randomness.\nRandom draws are statistically \"clumpy\": by chance, several waiters land in\nthe same time window, producing concurrency peaks larger than necessary. The\ngolden ratio is the most irrational number, so its additive recurrence\ndistributes points across the window as evenly as possible (Weyl\nequidistribution / three-distance theorem).\n\nThis offers three properties the random strategies cannot:\n\n1. **Bounded worst-case spread** — the peak concurrency across N uncoordinated\n   waiters is controlled, not luck-dependent.\n2. **Reproducibility** — identical runs produce identical schedules, which\n   makes retry behavior testable and debuggable (random jitter is not).\n3. **No RNG required** — useful where a stable per-waiter index is available\n   (host id, shard, worker number) but a strong RNG is not (embedded/IoT).\n\nThis is **complementary** to the random strategies, not a replacement. Where\ncallers cannot provide distinct indices, the random strategies remain the\nright default.\n\n## Benchmark\n\nThundering-herd simulation, peak concurrency (lower is better), same\nexponential window for both, 300 trials:\n\n| Scenario | Full Jitter (random) worst peak | Golden Jitter worst peak | Worst-case reduction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1000 clients / 50 slots | 45 (2.25× ideal) | 21 (1.05× ideal) | **53%** |\n| 10000 clients / 100 slots | 137 (1.37× ideal) | 102 (1.02× ideal) | **26%** |\n| 10000 clients / 200 slots | 82 (1.64× ideal) | 51 (1.02× ideal) | **38%** |\n\nMean peak is similar between the two; the gain is concentrated in the\n**worst case** and in **predictability** — which is what reliability\nengineering sizes for.\n\n## Honest caveats\n\n* The advantage is worst-case / tail behavior and reproducibility, not a\n  large average-case win.\n* It requires distinct `seq_index` values across waiters; with identical\n  indices it degenerates to a fixed schedule (documented in the docstring).\n* The benchmark is an idealized model; real-world clock skew and network\n  latency would shrink the gap. Reproducibility and no-RNG remain regardless.\n\n## Changes\n\n* `tenacity/wait.py`: add `wait_golden_jitter` class.\n* `tests/test_tenacity.py`: add `TestWaitGoldenJitter` (6 tests).\n* `doc/source/index.rst`: document the new strategy and when to prefer it.\n\n## Prior art\n\nThe use of the golden ratio for even, hard-to-resonate spacing is\nwell-established in low-discrepancy sampling. A formal optimality result for\ngolden-ratio scheduling in a related setting appears in Kempe, Schulman &\nTamuz, \"Quasi-regular sequences and optimal schedules for security games\"\n(SODA 2018). This PR applies the same principle to retry timing.", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/642/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/642/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/426", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/426/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/426/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/426/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/426", "id": 2045669999, "node_id": "PR_kwDOA-b4g85iNhHo", "number": 426, "title": "Improves wait_exponential_jitter", "user": {"login": "yxtay", "id": 5795122, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjU3OTUxMjI=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5795122?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/yxtay", "html_url": "https://github.com/yxtay", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yxtay/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yxtay/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yxtay/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yxtay/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yxtay/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yxtay/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yxtay/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yxtay/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yxtay/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 4, "created_at": "2023-12-18T03:38:03Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-11T18:38:24Z", "closed_at": "2026-03-11T18:38:24Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/pulls/426", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/426", "diff_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/426.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/426.patch", "merged_at": null}, "body": "# Summary\r\n\r\nImproves wait_exponential_jitter to inherit wait_exponential\r\n    - Reuses `wait_exponential.__call__` method instead of of duplicating code\r\n    - Follows argument names of wait_exponential\r\n    - Adds `min` argument\r\n    - Supports supplying `max`, `jitter`, `min` arguments as `timedelta`\r\n\r\n# Tests\r\n\r\n```\r\npytest tests/test_tenacity.py::TestWaitConditions::test_wait_exponential_jitter\r\n```", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/426/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/426/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/629", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/629/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/629/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/629/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/629", "id": 4058308395, "node_id": "PR_kwDOA-b4g87Jtp03", "number": 629, "title": "feat: deprecate `initial` in favor of `multiplier` in `wait_exponential_jitter`", "user": {"login": "jd", "id": 2644, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI2NDQ=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2644?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 2, "created_at": "2026-03-11T13:40:23Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-11T15:57:04Z", "closed_at": "2026-03-11T15:54:31Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "OWNER", "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/pulls/629", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/629", "diff_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/629.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/629.patch", "merged_at": "2026-03-11T15:54:31Z"}, "body": "Every other exponential wait class uses `multiplier`. Having `initial`\nonly on `wait_exponential_jitter` is confusing. Add `multiplier` param\nand deprecate `initial` as its alias.\n\n- Add `multiplier` parameter (default 1)\n- Emit `DeprecationWarning` when `initial` is used\n- Raise `ValueError` if both `initial` and `multiplier` are specified\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/629/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/629/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/628", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/628/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/628/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/628/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/628", "id": 4058308300, "node_id": "PR_kwDOA-b4g87Jtpzl", "number": 628, "title": "feat: add `min` param and `timedelta` support to `wait_exponential_jitter`", "user": {"login": "jd", "id": 2644, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI2NDQ=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2644?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 3, "created_at": "2026-03-11T13:40:22Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-11T14:25:36Z", "closed_at": "2026-03-11T14:20:45Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "OWNER", "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/pulls/628", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/628", "diff_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/628.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/628.patch", "merged_at": "2026-03-11T14:20:45Z"}, "body": "`wait_exponential` already supports `min` and `timedelta` for min/max.\n`wait_exponential_jitter` lacked both, which was an inconsistency users\nasked for in #426.\n\n- Accept `timedelta` for `max`, `jitter`, and `min` parameters\n- Add `min` parameter to set a minimum wait time floor\n- Convert all time parameters via `_utils.to_seconds()` in `__init__`\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/628/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/628/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/627", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/627/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/627/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/627/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/627", "id": 4058294688, "node_id": "PR_kwDOA-b4g87Jtm8T", "number": 627, "title": "feat: add `min` param and `timedelta` support to `wait_exponential_jitter`", "user": {"login": "jd", "id": 2644, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI2NDQ=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2644?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jd/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 0, "created_at": "2026-03-11T13:37:44Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-11T14:19:51Z", "closed_at": "2026-03-11T14:19:51Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "OWNER", "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": true, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/pulls/627", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/627", "diff_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/627.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/627.patch", "merged_at": null}, "body": "`wait_exponential` already supports `min` and `timedelta` for min/max.\n`wait_exponential_jitter` lacked both, which was an inconsistency users\nasked for in #426.\n\n- Accept `timedelta` for `max`, `jitter`, and `min` parameters\n- Add `min` parameter to set a minimum wait time floor\n- Convert all time parameters via `_utils.to_seconds()` in `__init__`\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/627/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/627/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/397", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/397/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/397/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/397/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/issues/397", "id": 1644357031, "node_id": "I_kwDOA-b4g85iAuWn", "number": 397, "title": "wait with proportional, but limited, jitter", "user": {"login": "moshez", "id": 422703, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQyMjcwMw==", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/422703?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/moshez", "html_url": "https://github.com/moshez", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/moshez/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/moshez/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/moshez/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/moshez/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/moshez/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/moshez/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/moshez/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/moshez/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/moshez/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 1, "created_at": "2023-03-28T17:09:17Z", "updated_at": "2026-02-24T06:23:58Z", "closed_at": "2026-02-24T06:23:58Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Currently, for exponential-backoff-with-jitter, you have two options:\r\n\r\n* A constant jitter (additive)\r\n* `random.uniform(0, exponential_wait_time)`\r\n\r\nIn my code, I like 10% jitter -- this way it is proportional, but is still somewhat predictable.\r\n\r\nThe way I do it from the outside is to define a waiter as follows:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nclass wait_proportional_jitter_exponential(tenacity.wait_exponential):\r\n    def __call__(self, retry_state: \"RetryCallState\") -> float:\r\n        goal = super().__call__(retry_state=retry_state)\r\n        return goal * random.uniform(0.9, 1.1)\r\n```\r\n\r\nWould this make sense to upstream? Probably not as-is, I'd make the `10%` an argument. Maybe this could be merged with `wait_random_exponential` by adding an argument `proportion`, so that the code would read\r\n\r\n```python\r\nclass wait_random_exponential(wait_exponential):\r\n    ...\r\n    def __call__(self, retry_state: \"RetryCallState\") -> float:\r\n        high = ...\r\n        return random.uniform(self.min_proprtion * high, high)\r\n```\r\n\r\n(I could pass in `min_proportion=0.9` for the behavior I need, and the default value could be `min_proportion=0` for the current behavior).\r\n\r\nLet me know if this makes sense, and if it does, whether you think it should be a new waiter or make an existing waiter more flexible, and I'll be happy to add a PR with code, docs, and unit tests.\r\n", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/397/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/397/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": "completed", "pinned_comment": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/223", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/223/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/223/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/223/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/issues/223", "id": 593523151, "node_id": "MDU6SXNzdWU1OTM1MjMxNTE=", "number": 223, "title": "Adding a \"Decorrelated Jitter\" wait class", "user": {"login": "ghost", "id": 10137, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/ghost", "html_url": "https://github.com/ghost", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 3, "created_at": "2020-04-03T17:10:25Z", "updated_at": "2026-02-19T14:38:50Z", "closed_at": "2026-02-19T14:38:50Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Hi, would it be possible to add a wait class corresponding to the \"Decorrelated Jitter\" algorithm described in https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/architecture/exponential-backoff-and-jitter/?\r\n\r\nI noticed that passing a `min` to the `wait_random_exponential` (https://github.com/jd/tenacity/issues/134) does not actually enforce a strict minimum for the wait times it produces. It seems to only set a minimum for the upper bound of the uniform distribution it samples from. Is that correct? I may also be missing something.\r\n\r\nI would like to enforce a strict minimum wait time since my use case involves hitting a service that has some heavy rate limits. I think the \"Decorrelated Jitter\" algorithm allows this while also being pretty much as effective as the \"Full Jitter\" algorithm.\r\n\r\nI'd also be happy to take a pass on trying to implement this if it seems like a worthy addition. Thanks!\r\n\r\n**Edit**\r\nI found this ticket which seems to be getting at a similar thing: https://github.com/jd/tenacity/issues/162.", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/223/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/223/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": "completed", "pinned_comment": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/106", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/106/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/106/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/106/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/issues/106", "id": 283555337, "node_id": "MDU6SXNzdWUyODM1NTUzMzc=", "number": 106, "title": "Disable `wait` for unittest", "user": {"login": "DanEEStar", "id": 1432939, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzI5Mzk=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1432939?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/DanEEStar", "html_url": "https://github.com/DanEEStar", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/DanEEStar/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/DanEEStar/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/DanEEStar/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/DanEEStar/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/DanEEStar/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/DanEEStar/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/DanEEStar/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/DanEEStar/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/DanEEStar/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [{"id": 426175559, "node_id": "MDU6TGFiZWw0MjYxNzU1NTk=", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/labels/documentation", "name": "documentation", "color": "fbca04", "default": true, "description": null}], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 18, "created_at": "2017-12-20T13:01:27Z", "updated_at": "2026-02-24T20:00:31Z", "closed_at": "2026-02-24T20:00:31Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "I am using the `@retry` decorator on a function which makes an HTTP-request.\r\n\r\nI am using this exact decorator call as an example:\r\n\r\n```\r\n@retry(stop=stop_after_attempt(7), wait=wait_random_exponential(multiplier=1, max=60))\r\ndef func():\r\n   ...\r\n   requests.post(...)\r\n```\r\n\r\nI have a unit tests which tests, that `func` does indeed get called multiple times when the post-request fails.\r\n\r\nBut it is a bit annoying that the test takes a long time.\r\n\r\nIs it possible to disable the `wait` time somehow only in the unit test to make the test faster?\r\nDo I have to mock a specific function?\r\n\r\nI also posted this on stackoverflow, in case you want some points :)\r\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/47906671/python-retry-with-tenacity-disable-wait-for-unittest\r\n", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/106/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/106/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": "completed", "pinned_comment": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/499", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/499/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/499/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/499/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/issues/499", "id": 2554836455, "node_id": "I_kwDOA-b4g86YR7Xn", "number": 499, "title": "[BUG] wait_exponential_jitter is not the sub class of wait_exponential, can't set max retry count", "user": {"login": "R0k1e", "id": 105703383, "node_id": "U_kgDOBkzn1w", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105703383?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/R0k1e", "html_url": "https://github.com/R0k1e", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/R0k1e/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/R0k1e/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/R0k1e/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/R0k1e/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/R0k1e/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/R0k1e/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/R0k1e/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/R0k1e/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/R0k1e/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 1, "created_at": "2024-09-29T09:34:29Z", "updated_at": "2025-02-25T01:51:11Z", "closed_at": "2025-02-25T01:51:11Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Questions as title, this is source code. Version 9.0.0\r\n``` python\r\nclass wait_exponential_jitter(wait_base):\r\n    \"\"\"Wait strategy that applies exponential backoff and jitter.\r\n\r\n    It allows for a customized initial wait, maximum wait and jitter.\r\n\r\n    This implements the strategy described here:\r\n    https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/retry-strategy\r\n\r\n    The wait time is min(initial * 2**n + random.uniform(0, jitter), maximum)\r\n    where n is the retry count.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(\r\n        self,\r\n        initial: float = 1,\r\n        max: float = _utils.MAX_WAIT,  # noqa\r\n        exp_base: float = 2,\r\n        jitter: float = 1,\r\n    ) -> None:\r\n        self.initial = initial\r\n        self.max = max\r\n        self.exp_base = exp_base\r\n        self.jitter = jitter\r\n\r\n    def __call__(self, retry_state: \"RetryCallState\") -> float:\r\n        jitter = random.uniform(0, self.jitter)\r\n        try:\r\n            exp = self.exp_base ** (retry_state.attempt_number - 1)\r\n            result = self.initial * exp + jitter\r\n        except OverflowError:\r\n            result = self.max\r\n        return max(0, min(result, self.max))\r\n```", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/499/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/499/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": "completed", "pinned_comment": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/393", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/393/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/393/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/393/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/393", "id": 1594832888, "node_id": "PR_kwDOA-b4g85Kf_SU", "number": 393, "title": "Add `retry_if_exception_cause_type` and `wait_exponential_jitter` to __all__", "user": {"login": "salmon131", "id": 48899038, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODk5MDM4", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48899038?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/salmon131", "html_url": "https://github.com/salmon131", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/salmon131/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/salmon131/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/salmon131/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/salmon131/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/salmon131/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/salmon131/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/salmon131/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/salmon131/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/salmon131/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 1, "created_at": "2023-02-22T10:17:47Z", "updated_at": "2023-02-22T16:17:59Z", "closed_at": "2023-02-22T16:17:58Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/pulls/393", "html_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/393", "diff_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/393.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/393.patch", "merged_at": "2023-02-22T16:17:58Z"}, "body": "Add omitted modules to import all.\r\n\r\n* related: https://github.com/jd/tenacity/pull/362", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/393/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jd/tenacity/issues/393/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason":